<title>USA: Fedders to buy back capital stock.</title>
<headline>Fedders to buy back capital stock.</headline>
<dateline>LIBERTY CORNER, N.J. 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fedders Corp said Tuesday its board of directors had approved a repurchase program of up to $50 million of any class of its outstanding capital stock.</p>
<p>&quot;Funding for the program will be provided by operating cash flow or debt financing,&quot; it said in a statement. &quot;This approval is in addition to the $25 million repurchase program authorized in 1996, which has been substantially completed.&quot;</p>
<p>The company's stock closed at 5-13/16 on Tuesday, up 2/16 from the previous day's close.</p>
<p>Fedders, which makes room air conditioners, has more than 40 million shares in circulation.</p>
